.TH GIT-SMV 1 "2026-05-19" "git-smv" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-smv \- Git Submodule Versioning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git smv
[\-h | \-\-help] [\-\-gitsmv-file <path>] <command> [<args>...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git smv
manages submodule versioning through a lock file \fB.gitsmv\fR at the repository root.
The lock file uses the same git-config format as \fB.gitmodules\fR but stores only
versioning metadata: \fBversion\fR, \fBref\fR, and \fBresolved\fR.
.PP
\fB.gitmodules\fR remains the source for \fBpath\fR, \fBurl\fR, and \fBbranch\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinit\fR
Create \fB.gitsmv\fR. With \fB\-\-from-gitmodules\fR, populate entries from current submodule state.
.TP
\fBadd\fR
Add a submodule and create a lock entry.
.TP
\fBremove\fR
Remove a submodule and its lock entry.
.TP
\fBlock\fR
Resolve refs and update \fBresolved\fR SHAs in \fB.gitsmv\fR.
.TP
\fBsync\fR
Check out submodules at \fBresolved\fR SHAs from \fB.gitsmv\fR.
.TP
\fBbump\fR
Update \fBref\fR and/or \fBversion\fR for a submodule.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show drift between lock, working tree, and parent gitlink.
.TP
\fBdiff\fR
Compare \fB.gitsmv\fR \fBresolved\fR values with parent gitlinks.
.SH FILES
.B .gitsmv
Lock file (git-config format).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITSMV_FILE
Override path to the lock file.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR git-submodule (1)
.BR gitmodules (5)
